hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16189","He said: Sufyan informed us, from Yahya ibn Said, he heard Bushayr ibn Yasar, the freedman of Banu Harithah. Sufyan said: This is the hadith of Ibn Hathmah, informing from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah. And Abdullah ibn Sahl of the Ansar was found slain in a well of the wells of Khaybar. So his uncles and brother came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): his brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, and his uncles Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah. Abd al-Rahman went to speak at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The elder, the elder. So one of his uncles spoke, either Huwayyisah or Muhayyisah. Sufyan said: I forgot which of them was the elder. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, we found Abdullah slain in a well of the wells of Khaybar. Then he mentioned the Jews and their evil and enmity. He said: Fifty of you shall swear that the Jews killed him. They said: How do we swear over what we did not see? He said: Then the Jews acquit you with fifty, swearing they did not kill him. They said: How do we accept their oaths while they are polytheists? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from himself, and a young she-camel of it kicked me. It was said to Sufyan: In the hadith: And you deserve the blood of your companion? He said: It is that."
"16190","He said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling dates for dates, and allowed araya to be bought by its estimate, its people eating it fresh. Sufyan said: Yahya ibn Said said to me: And what is the knowledge of the people of Makkah of araya? I said: Ata informed them, he heard it from Jabir."
"16191","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Masud ibn Niyar, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: He came to us while we were in our mosque. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you estimate, take and leave. Leave the third, and if you do not leave or harvest, Shubah is the doubter, the third, then the fourth."
"16192","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Masud ibn Niyar, he said: Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah came to us in our mosque and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you estimate, take and leave. Leave the third, and if you do not harvest or leave, then the fourth."
"16193","He said: Abd al-Quddus ibn Bakr ibn Khunays narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj informed us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, and al-Hajjaj, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from his uncle Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: Habibah daughter of Sahl was under Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas al-Ansari, and she disliked him, and he was an ugly man. So she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see him; were it not for fear of Allah Almighty I would spit in his face. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wilt thou return to him his garden which he dowered thee? She said: Yes. So he sent to him, and she returned to him his garden, and he separated between them. He said: So that was the first khul in Islam."
"16194","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated, from Ibn Ishaq, Bushayr ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, he said: Abdullah ibn Sahl, brother of Banu Harithah, went out among a group of Banu Harithah to Khaybar to fetch dates from it. He said: Abdullah ibn Sahl was assaulted, his neck broken, then thrown in a stream of the streams of the springs of Khaybar. His companions missed him and sought him until they found him, then buried him. He said: Then they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his brother Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came forward, and his cousins Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah, and they were elder than Abd al-Rahman, and Abd al-Rahman was then the foremost of the people and the owner of blood, so he stepped forward for that and spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before his cousins Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The elder, the elder. So Abd al-Rahman drew back, and Huwayyisah spoke, then Muhayyisah spoke, then Abd al-Rahman spoke. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, our companion was assaulted and killed, and there is in Khaybar no enemy but the Jews. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You name your killer, then swear over him fifty oaths, then he is surrendered. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, we would not swear over what we did not witness. He said: Then they swear to you fifty oaths and are acquitted of the blood of your companion. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we would not accept the oaths of the Jews; what they are in of disbelief is greater than that they swear over sin. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from himself, a hundred camels. Sahl says: By Allah, I do not forget a red young she-camel of them that kicked me while I drive it."
"16195","He said: Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafii narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Abu Layla ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, that Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah informed him, and men of the elders of his people, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Huwayyisah and Muhayyisah and Abd al-Rahman: Do you swear and deserve the blood of your companion? They said: No. He said: Then the Jews swear? They said: They are not Muslims. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paid his blood money from himself."
